+# Quantization & Low-memory Inference Guide
+
+This file documents recommended paths for low-memory inference:
+
+1) bitsandbytes (8-bit) + Hugging Face accelerate
+ - Use load_in_8bit=True and device_map="auto" for GPUs with tensor cores.
+ - Use bnb optimizers for finetuning with LoRA.
+
+2) GGML / gguf for CPU-only inference
+ - Convert model to ggml via tools (oss projects) and run via GGML inference runtime for edge/CPU.
+
+3) Triton + quantized checkpoints
+ - Export quantized model artifacts and place into Triton model repository; use reduced batch sizes and CPU offload.
+
+CI smoke tests:
+ - Validate output shape and basic logit sanity on a small prompt.
+ - Compare quantized output with fp16 model via cosine similarity or top-k overlap thresholds.
+
+Notes:
+ - Quantization reduces memory but may change outputs; always add fidelity tests and human-in-the-loop verification for critical tasks.
